"citation_ids":["cite.long.record-257bm-c7"],"evidence_ids":["mapping.long.record-257bm-c7"],"id":"long.record-257bm-c7","kind":"claim","label":"Long record Theorem 6.75 (Filling the remaining binary positions)","locator":"Long record Theorem 6.75, p. 66, label record:257bm-c7","source_id":"paper.long.pdf","statement":"*For any $c\\ge4$ and any finite $D\\subseteq[2,c)$ with $\\mathrm{value}(D)<1/2$ and the sharp capacity\n$$\n\\ensuremath{S}(D,1,2c-2) < 2^{c-2},\n$$\nthere is an exact row $E$ at endpoint $2c-2$ with $D\\subseteq E$ and every new rank strictly above $c$. The implication requires the displayed capacity bound, but neither a crossing condition nor a specified real greedy prefix. The crossing hypothesis used in Theorem 6.70 is one way to seek that input, not an additional premise of this filling result. No strict comparison between the corresponding cofinal existence statements is asserted.*","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:5d6514073ac52d75d011c84ff900912363a94ff7fe2e141210e6bf3c445c0cc1/nodes/long.record-257bm-c7","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:5d6514073ac52d75d011c84ff900912363a94ff7fe2e141210e6bf3c445c0cc1/nodes/long.record-257bm-c7","id":"sha256:5d6514073ac52d75d011c84ff900912363a94ff7fe2e141210e6bf3c445c0cc1/edges/%5B%22long.record-257bm-c7%22%2C%22lean.Erdos249257.exists_exactRowStrictUpperFill_of_skippedCoreSharpCapacity%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","kind":"formalizes","record_ref":"sha256:5d6514073ac52d75d011c84ff900912363a94ff7fe2e141210e6bf3c445c0cc1/edges/%5B%22long.record-257bm-c7%22%2C%22lean.Erdos249257.exists_exactRowStrictUpperFill_of_skippedCoreSharpCapacity%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","semantic_class":"formalization_correspondence","to":"sha256:5d6514073ac52d75d011c84ff900912363a94ff7fe2e141210e6bf3c445c0cc1/nodes/lean.Erdos249257.exists_exactRowStrictUpperFill_of_skippedCoreSharpCapacity"},{"derived":true,"family":"provenance","from":"sha256:5d6514073ac52d75d011c84ff900912363a94ff7fe2e141210e6bf3c445